static const char _zs3756_d[] = "a bare `if` here needs braces\n\nA `then` or `case` body is a primary-expression, and the two forms it excludes are exactly the two that can consume an `else`. Written bare, a following `else` would have two candidate owners -- this `if` and the enclosing one -- and would bind silently to the inner. Write `then { if ... }`. An `else` body carries no such ambiguity and takes an `if` bare, which is what `else if` is.";
